# TinyMUX's forms of functions and substitutions PennMUSH shares (TinyMUX compatibility). Each case is
# the parity case for its compatibility profile entry; the steps that differ are allowlisted in
# known-differences.json with both servers' output pinned. The last case runs the four mux_ options at
# their default, off, where SharpMUSH has to answer as PennMUSH does.

::case mux.login
::login wiz Wiz wizpass
think ok

::case mux.forms  TinyMUX's forms of shared functions: calls PennMUSH refuses are answered as TinyMUX does
think [switch(x,default)]|[add(5)]|[and(1)]|[lnum()]|[iter(a b,itext())]
think wrap(aaa bbb ccc,5,right)
think setunion(B a c,b, ,|,a)
think wrap(abc def,4,,|)
think setunion(c a b,b d, ,|)

::case mux.percent-m  %m is the running command, as in TinyMUX; PennMUSH has no %m and prints m
think %m|%c

::case mux.attribute-sub  %=<name> is the executor's attribute, as in TinyMUX; PennMUSH prints %= then <name>
&MUXSUB me=hello
think %=<muxsub>
&MUXSUB me=

::case mux.options-off  the mux_ options are off by default and SharpMUSH answers as PennMUSH
think [and(1,abc)]|[or(0,abc)]|[xor(1,1,1)]|[ljust(abcdef,3)]|[center(abcdefg,3)]|[sort(b A a B)]|[comp(a,B)]
think [gt(words(list(functions)),100)]
